        "v": "The adr.github.io site adds vocabulary. An architectural decision is a justified design choice that addresses a functional or non-functional requirement of architectural significance. An ADR captures a single such decision and its rationale. The collection of ADRs over a project's life is the decision log (ADL). An architecturally significant requirement (ASR) is one with a measurable effect on the architecture and quality of the system. [2]"
